INT. MARLIN HEIGHTS HIGH SCHOOL - GYMNASIUM - NIGHT

Bleachers half full. A banner: "STATE SEMIFINAL." The scoreboard reads 58-58 with 0:04 left. A buzzer hangs in the air.

COACH RUSTY CALHOUN, 50s, in a windbreaker and clipboard, crouches at the sideline in the huddle. TAMIKA BOONE, 17, the point guard, sweat-soaked jersey, kneels beside him. DMITRI VOLKOV, 18, the center, towers over both, towel around his neck.

COACH CALHOUN
Four seconds. Ball goes in at half-court. Tamika, you take it. Dmitri, screen.

TAMIKA
Coach, they'll double me.

DMITRI
(together with Tamika)
They'll double her.

^COACH CALHOUN
They'll double you.

All three stop. Dmitri grins. Tamika laughs, short, nervous.

COACH CALHOUN (CONT'D)
Then Dmitri slips the screen. Roll to the basket. Tamika, you hit him.

DMITRI
Over three defenders?

COACH CALHOUN
Over a hundred. You're seven feet of Ukrainian pride.

DMITRI
I'm six-eight.

COACH CALHOUN
And pride.

The horn sounds. They break the huddle. Calhoun grips Tamika's shoulder.

COACH CALHOUN (CONT'D)
Whatever happens, I'm proud of you.

TAMIKA
That's what you say before we lose.

COACH CALHOUN
That's what I say before we win, too.

The referee blows the whistle. Dmitri steps up. Tamika takes the ball at midcourt, faces the double team, and for one second looks at the rafters.

She whips the pass over the defenders' heads. Dmitri catches it at the rim, rises, and jams it through just as the horn blares.

The gym explodes. Calhoun drops his clipboard.

COACH CALHOUN (CONT'D)
(whispering)
Nobody tell them I cried.
